# The three files the user owns are shipped byte for byte.
#
# Without this, git's autocrlf conversion rewrites their line endings on a
# checkout: a fresh clone of this bundle on a Windows host turns them into CRLF
# and the bundle no longer carries the user's text verbatim. Marking them
# -text tells git to store the bytes as they are and restore them as they are.
prompt-overlay.md                       -text
swarm-prompt.md                         -text
skills/swarm-engineering/swarm-engineering.md -text

# The plugin's own markdown is kept the same way.
#
# The runtime note is composed into a prompt and the craft files are registered
# as skills, so their bytes are what a lane reads. A CRLF conversion would put
# a stray carriage return into every composed line, and it would make two
# checkouts of the same bundle differ.
runtime-note.md                    -text
README.md                          -text
skills/swarm-engineering/shared.md           -text
skills/swarm-engineering/developer.md        -text
skills/swarm-engineering/tester.md           -text
skills/swarm-engineering/reviewer.md         -text
skills/swarm-engineering/languages/python.md -text
